  "decision": "Adopt zstd0.13.3 without default features for a bounded baseline, not selected production codec. Resolved safe7.4.1 is BSD-3-Clause, sys2.1.3 is BSD-3-Clause AND BSD-2-Clause. Preserve MIT/BSD notices with installs. Use stream single_frame, exact remaining-input check, WindowLogMax26 and decoded length cap before native checksum/structural verification. Parquet, full-history streaming and real-data measurements remain pending.",
  "features": "zstd default-features=false; resolved zstd-safe/std and zstd-sys/std. No bindgen, dictionary builder, legacy decoding or codec worker threads. Bundled C uses existing cc with parallel build/jobserver; the Rust application introduces no unsafe blocks.",
  "build_notes": "New lock entries include jobserver/getrandom0.4/r-efi6 from cc parallel build support, not additional application RNG or runtime services. No TLS/signature/checksum verification bypass.",
